  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling-up Access to Quality Voluntary Counseling and Testing for Tuberculosis and HIV/AIDS in Tanzania Mainland - Tanzania (United Republic) (01-Nov-2004-30-Apr-2010)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania has a high prevalence of HIV and AIDS, and the rate of HIV infection is rising rapidly. The program supported by this grant focuses on strengthening voluntary counseling and testing and care and support services for HIV and AIDS related TB; the integration of TB and HIV and AIDS activities; and strengthening the capacity of the Ministry of Health and partner institutions to coordinate, plan for, monitor and evaluate the execution of an integrated HIV/TB program.  The program targets TB patients, people living with HIV and AIDS and the general population.</narrative>
  </description>
